{
  "description": "The data in the images is what you want this is a back-up tool CodeHawk \u2014 SiteHawk's ordinance superagent. Registry-first instant recall, then a single coordinated hunt: parallel source discovery, direct fetch with automatic OxyLabs escalation, structured extraction from the text it actually retrieved, an adversarial QC pass, and a cited write into the TelecomOrdinance registry. Anything it cannot prove goes to the admin review queue instead of being guessed at.Here is the formula ",
  "instructions": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nmunicode_scraper.py \u2014 Telecom Ordinance Extractor\n==================================================\nExtracts ONLY telecommunications-related ordinance sections from\na municipality's Municode site via the public REST API.\n\nUsage:\n  python municode_scraper.py --city \"Cocoa\" --state FL\n  python municode_scraper.py --url \"https://library.municode.com/fl/cocoa/codes/code_of_ordinances\"\n  python municode_scraper.py --client-id 12345\n  python municode_scraper.py --city \"Palm Coast\" --state FL --output json\n  python municode_scraper.py --city \"Ocala\" --state FL --output txt\n\nOutputs:\n  - txt  : plain-text dump of matched sections (default)\n  - json : structured JSON with section metadata + text\n\nNo API keys required. No auth. No Selenium.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re, json, sys, time, argparse\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Tuple, Optional\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse, parse_qs\n\nimport httpx\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Config \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nAPI = \"https://api.municode.com\"\nTIMEOUT = 30.0\nSLEEP = 0.3  # polite delay between API calls\n\nTELECOM_KEYWORDS = [\n    \"wireless\", \"telecommunications\", \"tower\", \"antenna\", \"small cell\",\n    \"wcf\", \"wts\", \"communication facility\", \"cellular\", \"base station\",\n    \"monopole\", \"stealth\", \"camouflage\",\n]\n\nSEARCH_TERMS = [\n    \"telecommunications tower\",\n    \"wireless facility\",\n    \"communication tower\",\n    \"antenna\",\n    \"cell tower\",\n    \"small cell\",\n]\n\n# \u2500\u2500 API helpers \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\ndef api_get(path: str, params: dict = None) -> dict:\n    with httpx.Client(timeout=TIMEOUT) as c:\n        r = c.get(f\"{API}{path}\", params=params)\n        r.raise_for_status()\n        return r.json()\n\n\ndef html2text(h: str) -> str:\n    h = re.sub(r\"<br\\s*/?>\", \"\\n\", h, flags=re.I)\n    h = re.sub(r\"</?(?:p|div)[^>]*>\", \"\\n\", h, flags=re.I)\n    h = re.sub(r\"<[^>]+>\", \"\", h)\n    for ent, ch in [(\"&nbsp;\", \" \"), (\"&amp;\", \"&\"), (\"&lt;\", \"<\"),\n                    (\"&gt;\", \">\"), (\"&#8217;\", \"'\"), (\"&#8220;\", '\"'),\n                    (\"&#8221;\", '\"')]:\n        h = h.replace(ent, ch)\n    return re.sub(r\"\\n{3,}\", \"\\n\\n\", h).strip()\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 State / Municipality resolution \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n_STATES: Dict[str, int] = {}\n\ndef state_id(abbr: str) -> int:\n    global _STATES\n    if not _STATES:\n        _STATES = {s[\"StateAbbreviation\"]: s[\"StateID\"] for s in api_get(\"/states\")}\n    return _STATES.get(abbr.upper(), 0)\n\n\ndef find_client_id(city: str, state_abbr: str) -> Tuple[Optional[int], Optional[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Find client ID by city name + state. Returns (client_id, client_name).\"\"\"\n    sid = state_id(state_abbr)\n    if not sid:\n        return None, None\n    munis = api_get(f\"/Clients/stateId/{sid}\")\n    city_lower = city.lower().strip()\n    # Exact match first\n    for m in munis:\n        if m[\"ClientName\"].lower().strip() == city_lower:\n            return m[\"ClientID\"], m[\"ClientName\"]\n    # Substring match\n    for m in munis:\n        if city_lower in m[\"ClientName\"].lower():\n            return m[\"ClientID\"], m[\"ClientName\"]\n    return None, None\n\n\ndef parse_municode_url(url: str) -> Optional[int]:\n    \"\"\"Try to extract client_id from a Municode library URL.\"\"\"\n    # Pattern: library.municode.com/{state}/{city}/...\n    # We need to search by the city/state slug\n    parsed = urlparse(url)\n    parts = [p for p in parsed.path.strip(\"/\").split(\"/\") if p]\n    if len(parts) >= 2:\n        state_abbr = parts[0].upper()\n        city_slug = parts[1].replace(\"_\", \" \").replace(\"-\", \" \")\n        cid, _ = find_client_id(city_slug, state_abbr)\n        return cid\n    # Check for ?client_id= param\n    qs = parse_qs(parsed.query)\n    if \"client_id\" in qs:\n        return int(qs[\"client_id\"][0])\n    return None\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Product / Job resolution \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\ndef resolve_products(client_id: int) -> List[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"Returns [(productId, jobId, productName), ...]\"\"\"\n    results = []\n    try:\n        prods = api_get(f\"/Products/clientId/{client_id}\")\n        for p in (prods or []):\n            pid = p[\"ProductID\"]\n            try:\n                job = api_get(f\"/Jobs/latest/{pid}\")\n                results.append((pid, job[\"Id\"], p.get(\"ProductName\", \"\")))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return results\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Content fetching \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\ndef get_content(pid: int, jid: int, node_id: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        data = api_get(\"/CodesContent\", {\"productId\": pid, \"jobId\": jid, \"nodeId\": node_id})\n        parts = []\n        for doc in data.get(\"Docs\", []):\n            title = doc.get(\"Title\", \"\")\n            content = doc.get(\"Content\", \"\")\n            if content:\n                txt = html2text(content)\n                parts.append(f\"=== {title} ===\\n{txt}\" if title else txt)\n        return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)[:80000]\n    except Exception:\n        return \"\"\n\n\ndef get_toc_recursive(pid: int, jid: int, nodes: list, depth: int = 0,\n                      max_depth: int = 4) -> List[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Flatten TOC tree into a list of {id, heading, depth}.\"\"\"\n    flat = []\n    for node in nodes:\n        flat.append({\n            \"id\": node.get(\"Id\", \"\"),\n            \"heading\": node.get(\"Heading\", \"\"),\n            \"depth\": depth,\n            \"has_children\": node.get(\"HasChildren\", False),\n        })\n        if node.get(\"HasChildren\") and depth < max_depth:\n            children = node.get(\"Children\")\n            if not children:\n                # Fetch children via TOC endpoint with parent\n                try:\n                    child_data = api_get(\"/codesToc\", {\n                        \"productId\": pid, \"jobId\": jid, \"nodeId\": node[\"Id\"]\n                    })\n                    children = child_data.get(\"Children\", [])\n                except Exception:\n                    children = []\n            if children:\n                flat.extend(get_toc_recursive(pid, jid, children, depth + 1, max_depth))\n    return flat\n\n\ndef matches_telecom(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if text contains any telecom keyword.\"\"\"\n    lower = text.lower()\n    return any(kw in lower for kw in TELECOM_KEYWORDS)\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Main scrape logic \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\ndef scrape_telecom(client_id: int, client_name: str, verbose: bool = True) -> List[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Scrape all telecom-related ordinance sections for a municipality.\n    Returns list of {node_id, heading, product, text}.\n    \"\"\"\n    products = resolve_products(client_id)\n    if not products:\n        if verbose:\n            print(f\"  \u26a0\ufe0f  No products found for {client_name}\")\n        return []\n\n    results = []\n    seen_nodes = set()\n\n    for pid, jid, pname in products:\n        if verbose:\n            print(f\"  \ud83d\udcd6 Product: {pname} (pid={pid})\")\n\n        # \u2500\u2500 Strategy 1: Search API \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n        for term in SEARCH_TERMS:\n            try:\n                data = api_get(\"/search\", {\n                    \"searchText\": term,\n                    \"clientId\": client_id,\n                    \"contentTypeId\": \"CODES\",\n                    \"searchMode\": \"CLIENTMODE\",\n                })\n                for hit in (data.get(\"Hits\") or []):\n                    nid = hit.get(\"NodeId\")\n                    heading = hit.get(\"Heading\", \"\")\n                    if not nid or nid in seen_nodes:\n                        continue\n                    seen_nodes.add(nid)\n                    content = get_content(pid, jid, nid)\n                    if content and len(content) > 30 and matches_telecom(content):\n                        results.append({\n                            \"node_id\": nid,\n                            \"heading\": heading,\n                            \"product\": pname,\n                            \"product_id\": pid,\n                            \"text\": content,\n                        })\n                        if verbose:\n                            print(f\"    \u2705 [{term}] {heading} ({len(content):,} chars)\")\n                time.sleep(SLEEP)\n            except Exception as e:\n                if verbose:\n                    print(f\"    \u26a0\ufe0f  Search '{term}': {e}\")\n\n        # \u2500\u2500 Strategy 2: Browse TOC for telecom/zoning chapters \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n        if verbose:\n            print(f\"  \ud83d\udd0d Scanning TOC for telecom chapters...\")\n        try:\n            toc = api_get(\"/codesToc\", {\"productId\": pid, \"jobId\": jid})\n            top_nodes = toc.get(\"Children\", [])\n            flat_toc = get_toc_recursive(pid, jid, top_nodes, max_depth=3)\n\n            for node in flat_toc:\n                nid = node[\"id\"]\n                heading = node[\"heading\"]\n                if nid in seen_nodes:\n                    continue\n                if matches_telecom(heading):\n                    seen_nodes.add(nid)\n                    content = get_content(pid, jid, nid)\n                    if content and len(content) > 30:\n                        results.append({\n                            \"node_id\": nid,\n                            \"heading\": heading,\n                            \"product\": pname,\n                            \"product_id\": pid,\n                            \"text\": content,\n                        })\n                        if verbose:\n                            print(f\"    \u2705 [TOC] {heading} ({len(content):,} chars)\")\n                    time.sleep(SLEEP)\n        except Exception as e:\n            if verbose:\n                print(f\"    \u26a0\ufe0f  TOC scan: {e}\")\n\n    # Deduplicate by content similarity (exact text match)\n    unique = []\n    seen_text = set()\n    for r in results:\n        sig = r[\"text\"][:500]\n        if sig not in seen_text:\n            seen_text.add(sig)\n            unique.append(r)\n\n    return unique\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 Output formatters \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\ndef format_txt(client_name: str, state: str, sections: List[dict]) -> str:\n    lines = [\n        f\"{'='*70}\",\n        f\"  TELECOM ORDINANCE EXTRACT: {client_name}, {state}\",\n        f\"  Sections found: {len(sections)}\",\n        f\"  Scraped: {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')}\",\n        f\"{'='*70}\",\n        \"\",\n    ]\n    for i, s in enumerate(sections, 1):\n        lines.append(f\"{'\u2500'*70}\")\n        lines.append(f\"  Section {i}: {s['heading']}\")\n        lines.append(f\"  Product: {s['product']}  |  Node: {s['node_id']}\")\n        lines.append(f\"{'\u2500'*70}\")\n        lines.append(s[\"text\"])\n        lines.append(\"\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\ndef format_json(client_name: str, state: str, client_id: int,\n                sections: List[dict]) -> str:\n    return json.dumps({\n        \"municipality\": client_name,\n        \"state\": state,\n        \"client_id\": client_id,\n        \"scraped_at\": time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'),\n        \"section_count\": len(sections),\n        \"sections\": [\n            {\n                \"node_id\": s[\"node_id\"],\n                \"heading\": s[\"heading\"],\n                \"product\": s[\"product\"],\n                \"product_id\": s[\"product_id\"],\n                \"char_count\": len(s[\"text\"]),\n                \"text\": s[\"text\"],\n            }\n            for s in sections\n        ],\n    }, indent=2)\n\n\n# \u2500\u2500 CLI \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Municode Telecom Ordinance Scraper \u2014 extracts only telecom sections\"\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--city\", help=\"Municipality name (e.g. 'Cocoa', 'Palm Coast')\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--state\", help=\"Two-letter state abbreviation (e.g. FL)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--url\", help=\"Municode library URL\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--client-id\", type=int, help=\"Municode client ID directly\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--output\", choices=[\"txt\", \"json\"], default=\"txt\",\n                    help=\"Output format (default: txt)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Save output to file path\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Suppress progress output\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    verbose = not args.quiet\n    client_id = args.client_id\n    client_name = None\n    state_abbr = args.state\n\n    # Resolve client ID\n    if args.url:\n        if verbose:\n            print(f\"\ud83d\udd17 Parsing URL: {args.url}\")\n        client_id = parse_municode_url(args.url)\n        if not client_id:\n            print(\"\u274c Could not resolve client ID from URL. Try --city + --state.\")\n            sys.exit(1)\n\n    elif args.city and args.state:\n        if verbose:\n            print(f\"\ud83d\udd0d Searching for {args.city}, {args.state}...\")\n        client_id, client_name = find_client_id(args.city, args.state)\n        state_abbr = args.state.upper()\n        if not client_id:\n            print(f\"\u274c Municipality '{args.city}' not found in {args.state} on Municode.\")\n            sys.exit(1)\n\n    elif not client_id:\n        print(\"\u274c Provide --city + --state, --url, or --client-id\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    # Get client info if we don't have the name yet\n    if not client_name:\n        try:\n            info = api_get(f\"/clients/{client_id}\")\n            client_name = info.get(\"ClientName\", f\"Client {client_id}\")\n            if not state_abbr:\n                state_abbr = info.get(\"State\", {}).get(\"StateAbbreviation\", \"??\")\n        except Exception:\n            client_name = f\"Client {client_id}\"\n            state_abbr = state_abbr or \"??\"\n\n    if verbose:\n        print(f\"\\n\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f  {client_name} ({state_abbr})  \u2014  client_id={client_id}\")\n        print(f\"{'\u2500'*50}\")\n\n    # Scrape\n    sections = scrape_telecom(client_id, client_name, verbose=verbose)\n\n    if not sections:\n        print(\"\\n\u26a0\ufe0f  No telecom-related ordinance sections found.\")\n        sys.exit(0)\n\n    # Format output\n    if args.output == \"json\":\n        output = format_json(client_name, state_abbr, client_id, sections)\n    else:\n        output = format_txt(client_name, state_abbr, sections)\n\n    # Save or print\n    if args.save:\n        with open(args.save, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(output)\n        if verbose:\n            print(f\"\\n\ud83d\udcbe Saved to {args.save}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"\\n\" + output)\n\n    if verbose:\n        total_chars = sum(len(s[\"text\"]) for s in sections)\n        print(f\"\\n{'='*50}\")\n        print(f\"  \u2705 {len(sections)} telecom sections  |  {total_chars:,} total chars\")\n        print(f\"{'='*50}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
  "tool_configs": [
    {
      "entity_name": "TelecomOrdinance",
      "allowed_operations": [
        "read"
      ]
    },
    {
      "function_name": "codehawkHunt",
      "description": "The full CodeHawk pipeline for one jurisdiction: registry-first recall, then parallel source discovery, direct fetch with automatic OxyLabs escalation, cited extraction, QC, and a gated write. Args: { jurisdiction, state, force_refresh?, dry_run? }."
    },
    {
      "function_name": "zoneResolve",
      "description": "Resolve the governing jurisdiction, county, and state from site coordinates."
    },
    {
      "function_name": "oxylabsScrape",
      "description": "Rendered scrape of a specific municipal code URL the user supplies. Returns the page content \u2014 hand that content to extractTelecomOrdinance as ordinance_text rather than starting a new search."
    },
    {
      "function_name": "extractTelecomOrdinance",
      "description": "Structured telecom ordinance extraction. Pass ordinance_text (plus jurisdiction, state, source_url) to extract directly from text you already have; pass lat/lon only when you have no text and need the full research cascade."
    },
    {
      "function_name": "notionSaveOrdinance",
      "description": "Archive an extracted ordinance summary as a page in the Notion zoning knowledge base."
    }
  ],
